# Practical 2: Host Discovery

## Objective

Check whether a host is alive.

### Command

```bash
sudo nmap -sn 192.168.1.10
```

### Flag Explanation

| Flag | Meaning |
|--------|----------|
| -s | Scan |
| -n | No Port Scan |

### What Nmap Does

```text
Sends discovery packets
Checks if host responds
No port scanning performed
```

### Output Shows

```text
Host is up
Latency
MAC Address (sometimes)
```

