# Practical 4: SYN Scan (Stealth Scan)

## Command

```bash
sudo nmap -sS -p 1-1000 192.168.1.10
```

### Flag Explanation

| Flag | Meaning |
|--------|----------|
| -sS | SYN Scan |
| -p | Port Selection |
| 1-1000 | Scan ports 1 through 1000 |

### What Nmap Does

```text
Sends SYN packet
Checks response
Does not complete TCP handshake
```

### Output Shows

```text
Open Ports
Closed Ports
Filtered Ports
```

---

# Practical 5: TCP Connect Scan

## Command

```bash
sudo nmap -sT -p 22,80 192.168.1.10
```

### Flag Explanation

| Flag | Meaning |
|--------|----------|
| -sT | TCP Connect Scan |
| -p | Selected Ports |

### What Nmap Does

```text
Completes full TCP handshake
More visible than SYN scan
```

### Output Shows

```text
Port Number
State
Service Name
```

Example:

```text
22/tcp open ssh
80/tcp open http
```

